Haan, ye possible hai. Aapka exact setup ye ho sakta hai:

Google Form → Google Sheet → Apps Script → WhatsApp API → aapke WhatsApp number se message

Agar aap free + open-source + apna WhatsApp number use karna chahte hain, to main Evolution API recommend karunga. Ye open-source hai, self-host ho sakta hai aur WhatsApp Web/Baileys ke through message bhej sakta hai.

Best option: Evolution API

Evolution API – GitHub

Aapka flow:

Google Form
    ↓
Google Sheet
    ↓
Apps Script onFormSubmit()
    ↓
HTTP POST
    ↓
Evolution API
    ↓
Your WhatsApp Number
    ↓
Customer ko WhatsApp Message

Evolution API me QR code se WhatsApp connect kiya ja sakta hai, aur connected number se REST API ke through text message bheja ja sakta hai.

Step 1 — WhatsApp Web login

Aapko pehle Evolution API apne computer/server par chalani hogi.

Agar aap Windows computer use kar rahe ho, easiest method Docker Desktop hai. Evolution API officially Docker deployment provide karta hai.

Uske baad browser me Evolution API ka panel/API open hoga aur:

Create Instance → QR Code → WhatsApp phone → Linked Devices → Link a device

QR scan kar dena.

Yaani WhatsApp account aapke phone ka hi rahega, bas WhatsApp Web ki tarah API se connected hoga.

Step 2 — Google Sheet

Maan lo Form response Sheet me:

Timestamp	Name	Mobile	Message
19/08/2026	Rahul	9876543210	Product enquiry
Step 3 — Apps Script

Google Sheet me:

Extensions → Apps Script

phir ye code:


function onFormSubmit(e) {

  const row = e.values;

  const name = row[1];
  const mobile = row[2];

  const message =
    "Hello " + name + ",\n\n" +
    "Thank you for contacting us.\n" +
    "We have received your enquiry.\n\n" +
    "Regards,\n" +
    "Calco Poly Technik Pvt Ltd";

  const apiUrl =
    "http://YOUR_SERVER_IP:8080/message/sendText/YOUR_INSTANCE";

  const apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY";

  const payload = {
    number: "91" + mobile,
    options: {
      delay: 1200,
      presence: "composing"
    },
    textMessage: {
      text: message
    }
  };

  const options = {
    method: "post",
    contentType: "application/json",
    headers: {
      "apikey": apiKey
    },
    payload: JSON.stringify(payload),
    muteHttpExceptions: true
  };

  const response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(apiUrl, options);

  Logger.log(response.getContentText());
}

Evolution API ka text-message endpoint POST /message/sendText/[instance] hai aur request me number aur text diya jata hai.

Step 4 — Trigger lagana

Apps Script me:

Triggers → Add Trigger

Select:

Function:
onFormSubmit


Event source:
From spreadsheet


Event type:
On form submit

Ab jab bhi Google Form submit hoga:


Form → Sheet → Apps Script → Evolution API → WhatsApp

automatically message chala jayega.

⚠️ Sabse important: "free browser login"

Agar aapka matlab hai:

"Main koi paid WhatsApp API nahi lena chahta. Browser me QR scan karunga aur apne normal WhatsApp se message jayega."

Haan, ye Evolution API ke WhatsApp-Web/Baileys method se ho sakta hai. Official Meta Cloud API se ye same setup nahi hai. Evolution API khud bhi warn karta hai ki WhatsApp-Web-based method official API ki comparison me limitations rakh sakta hai.

Aapke case me main aapko next step me Windows PC par Evolution API ko completely free setup karwa sakta hoon — Docker install se lekar QR scan aur phir Google Sheet Apps Script tak.


Step 1 — WhatsApp Web login

Aapko pehle Evolution API apne computer/server par chalani hogi.

Agar aap Windows computer use kar rahe ho, easiest method Docker Desktop hai. Evolution API officially Docker deployment provide karta hai.

Uske baad browser me Evolution API ka panel/API open hoga aur:

Create Instance → QR Code → WhatsApp phone → Linked Devices → Link a device

QR scan kar dena.

ye batao step by step kese step kare

Bilkul. Chaliye Windows PC par zero se setup karte hain. Main aapko ek-ek step dunga; pehle Evolution API ko locally chalayenge, phir WhatsApp QR scan, uske baad Google Apps Script connect karenge.

Important correction: current Evolution API docs me Docker image/configuration me changes aaye hain, isliye main current official documentation ke according setup bata raha hoon. Evolution API open-source hai aur Baileys-based WhatsApp Web connection support karta hai.



STEP 1 — Docker Desktop install karo

Windows PC par browser kholo aur official Docker Desktop download karo:

Docker Desktop for Windows — Official

Docker Desktop Windows par WSL 2 backend ke saath use kiya ja sakta hai.

Install karne ke baad
Docker Desktop Installer.exe open karo.
Installation ke time Use WSL 2 instead of Hyper-V option selected rehne do.
Installation complete karo.
Docker Desktop open karo.
Agar terms/acceptance aaye to Accept karo.
Docker Desktop me whale icon running hona chahiye.

Docker ki official documentation bhi WSL 2 ko recommended/default backend batati hai.

STEP 2 — Check karo Docker properly chal raha hai

Windows me:

Start → PowerShell

open karo.

Ye command likho:

docker --version

Aisa kuch aana chahiye:

Docker version xx.x.x

Phir:

docker ps

Agar table aa jaye aur koi error nahi aaye, Docker ready hai.


STEP 3 — Evolution API folder banao

Desktop par ek folder banao:

EvolutionAPI

Example:

C:\EvolutionAPI

Ab PowerShell me:

cd C:\EvolutionAPI


STEP 4 — .env file banao

Notepad kholo aur ye likho:

AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=AkashEvolution2026@123456

File ko save karo:

C:\EvolutionAPI\.env

⚠️ Dhyan rahe file ka naam:

.env

ho, .env.txt nahi.

STEP 5 — Evolution API start karo

Ab PowerShell me ye command chalao:

docker pull evoapicloud/evolution-api:latest

Current Evolution API repository Docker ke liye evoapicloud/evolution-api:latest image provide karti hai.

Download complete hone ke baad:

docker run -d --name evolution_api -p 8080:8080 --env-file C:\EvolutionAPI\.env evoapicloud/evolution-api:latest

Thoda wait karo.

Phir:

docker ps

Aapko evolution_api naam ka container running dikhna chahiye.

STEP 6 — Browser me check karo

Chrome kholo aur ye address:

Evolution API local server

Agar API correctly start ho gayi hai to response/API page milna chahiye.

Official Docker documentation ke according local deployment ko http://localhost:8080 par access karke verify kiya ja sakta hai.

STEP 7 — Swagger/API page kholo

Browser me:

Evolution API Swagger


open karo.

Yahan Evolution API ke endpoints milenge.

STEP 8 — WhatsApp Instance create karna

Ab hum WhatsApp connect karenge.

Evolution API me instance create karne ke liye endpoint available hai:

POST /instance/create

Aur WhatsApp Web/Baileys integration ke liye:

integration: WHATSAPP-BAILEYS

use hota hai. QR code generation bhi supported hai.

Swagger me:

Instance → POST /instance/create

open karo.

Try it out dabao.

Body me approximately:

{
  "instanceName": "calco-whatsapp",
  "integration": "WHATSAPP-BAILEYS",
  "qrcode": true
}

bhejna hoga.

Lekin yahan ek important point hai: aapke installed Evolution API version ke hisaab se exact Swagger fields/version differ ho sakte hain. Isliye blindly next command nahi dena chahta.

Abhi aap sirf ye 3 steps karo:

1. Docker Desktop install karo

2. PowerShell me:

docker --version

3. Phir:

docker pull evoapicloud/evolution-api:latest

Uske baad mujhe PowerShell ka screenshot bhej do.

Main uske baad aapko STEP 2: Evolution API start → browser me open → instance create → QR code → phone se WhatsApp scan exactly aapke screen ke according karwaunga.


Uske baad final me:

Google Form → Google Sheet → Apps Script → WhatsApp automatic message

bhi connect kar denge.

PS C:\Users\ASUS> docker --version
Docker version 29.7.2, build a7dcaa6
PS C:\Users\ASUS> STEP 3 — Evolution API folder banao
Desktop par ek folder banao:

EvolutionAPI

Example:

C:\EvolutionAPI

Ab PowerShell me:

cd C:\EvolutionAPI
STEP 4 — .env file banao

Notepad kholo aur ye likho:

AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=AkashEvolution2026@123456

File ko save karo:

C:\EvolutionAPI\.env

⚠️ Dhyan rahe file ka naam:

.env

ho, .env.txt nahi. step 3 or 4 cmd se karte hai

Haan, Step 3 aur Step 4 dono CMD/PowerShell se hi kar sakte hain. Aap abhi PowerShell me ho, to wahi se karo.

STEP 3 — Folder CMD/PowerShell se banao

Ab ye command chalao:

mkdir C:\EvolutionAPI

Phir folder me jao:

cd C:\EvolutionAPI

Check karne ke liye:

pwd

Output ye hona chahiye:

Path
----
C:\EvolutionAPI
STEP 4 — .env file CMD/PowerShell se banao

Ab ye command chalao:

Set-Content -Path "C:\EvolutionAPI\.env" -Value "AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=AkashEvolution2026@123456"

Ab check karo:

Get-ChildItem -Force

Aapko:

.env

dikhna chahiye.

.env ke andar kya hai check karna ho
Get-Content C:\EvolutionAPI\.env

Output:

AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=AkashEvolution2026@123456


Abhi tak complete

Aapke paas:

C:\
└── EvolutionAPI
    └── .env

hona chahiye.

Abhi Docker run mat karo. Pehle ye commands chalao:

mkdir C:\EvolutionAPI
cd C:\EvolutionAPI
Set-Content -Path "C:\EvolutionAPI\.env" -Value "AUTHENTICATION_API_KEY=AkashEvolution2026@123456"
Get-ChildItem -Force
Get-Content C:\EvolutionAPI\.env

